er ruling. (3) The same witness has y0_star, y_star, dual_obj, duality_gap all null with the status string 'STUB — re-run script through lp_dual_solver.py to populate', so it does not satisfy the AGENTS.md LP/SDP first-class-dual requirement it is subject to. It also records gram_det = -0.1892052530713217, i.e. NONZERO, while its sibling block prf:knot-operator-selection asserts 'on H_n itself det G = 0 exactly'. Those two statements are consistent only if one is convention-C and the other convention-D — which is exactly the split I measure — so the chapter is carrying both conventions at once. (4) DISPLAYED ARITHMETIC DOES NOT REPRODUCE: 'E_0 = 0.782/0.1883 approx 4.155 MeV' — the printed division gives 4.1529, not 4.155. The RESULT is right (the witness has E0_MeV = 4.154925) because it was computed from Q = 0.7823334 and |Delta net| = 0.18829062; it is the rounded display that fails to reproduce it. Proposed: quote 0.78233/0.18829. (5) CIRCULARITY, stated as a verification: 'The six terms sum exactly to Q_beta.' E_0 is DEFINED as Q_beta/|Delta net| and Delta net is by the block's own linearity clause the sum of the six coefficient differences, so sum_i Delta_i E_0 = Q_beta identically. That is the definition unfolded, not a check, and it should not be presented as one. Related: 'Untyped composition yields net approx 1.506. The CODATA proton net is approx 0.999. Typed crossings close this gap.' — CODATA measures masses, not 'nets'; 0.999 is a target, and the typed-crossing shift h_A is introduced to reach it, landing on 0.9991. That is the shape of a fit and should be labelled per the production-vs-exploratory discipline. Two lesser notes: the bold banner '**Full derivation.**' is followed by three summary sentences that derive nothing (the dangling-banner pattern); and the block says 'CODATA 2022' while its witness carries CODATA-2018 masses (m_p = 938.27208816 against the 2022 value 938.27208943). The witness's own auditOnly pointer, docs/audits/categorical-vs-fitted-q-decay-ba.md, does not exist.","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","history":2},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"uses-formal-coverage","group":"uses","result":"n/a","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","notes":"block has no .lean sibling","history":1},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","history":1},{"id":"voice-ai-slop","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-07-19","reviewer":"agent","by":"one-voice-audit","notes":"Agentic heuristic check: pass.","history":2},{"id":"voice-author-notes-pollution","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","history":1},{"id":"voice-branch-jargon","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"unknown","changed":["md: on disk, no hash recorded","ts: on disk, no hash recorded"],"at":"2026-08-08","reviewer":"agent","by":"local/one-voice-audit","notes":"[EXPIRED-NO-FIELD-HASH] No branch/audit working labels, agent status markers or first-person work narration found in the .md 